# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# /salud/* is an animal's veterinary record, handed by a rescuer to the family
# that adopted or is fostering them. It is reachable by link on purpose — a
# link in a family's WhatsApp has to keep working for years — but it has no
# business in a search index. The page sets <meta name="robots"> once React
# mounts and the API sends X-Robots-Tag on its JSON, but a crawler that does
# not run JS sees neither: this header is the one that reaches it, because
# Pages serves the SPA shell for the path itself.
/salud/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
